SYS=LLMDDv6.0
MODE=ITR_EXEC_IR
TENSOR.GRAMMAR=KEY=VALUE or NAMESPACE.KEY=VALUE — one complete semantic unit per line
TENSOR.SEPARATORS== assignment, . namespace, , list, > flow, X exchange, ${} env expansion, -> relation arrow, | item separator
TENSOR.SELF_CONTAINED=True — no external references, no config files, no docs needed
TENSOR.LEGEND=Every ITR must include a LEGEND line defining all symbols used, so the coder never needs external context
NODE.X=EXTRACTOR
NODE.X_DESC=Reads working tree, builds DTR with files, types, relations, constraints
NODE.DTR=DESIGN_TENSOR_TRIPLE
NODE.DTR_DESC=Structured codebase snapshot: addressable map of files, classes, interfaces, and relations
NODE.ADV=ADVISOR
NODE.ADV_DESC=Receives DTR, analyzes structure, brainstorms with designer, emits ITR on approval. Writes ITR to itr-buffer/<app>.itr and commits it. Never writes application code.
NODE.DSG=DESIGNER
NODE.DSG_DESC=Human. Extracts DTR or runs baseline-generator, discusses with advisor, gives green light to emit ITR.
NODE.ITR=IMPLEMENTATION_TENSOR
NODE.ITR_DESC=Work order of Computational Units (CUs). Defines targeted DTR addresses, instructions, and expected DTR delta additions (NEW_DTR_LINES) for verification. Overwritten each iteration, lineage in git.
NODE.COD=CODER
NODE.COD_DESC=Receives CU-based ITR and baseline DTR. Implements CUs in dependency order. Generates feedback and commits everything using the commit tool with their own summary message.
NODE.OUT=OUTPUT
NODE.OUT_DESC=Produced code, updated DTR, and FEEDBACK file. Updated DTR is statically verified against baseline DTR + DTR delta.
21: FLOW=X>DTR>ADV X DSG>ITR>COD>OUT>DTR
FLOW.FEEDBACK=COD>FEEDBACK>ADV — feedback flows back to Advisor for ITR optimization
FSM=ANALYZE X DECIDE>EMIT_ITR
DTR=MODE,STATE,FILES,TYPE_MAP,RELATIONS,CONSTRAINTS,META
ITR=LEGEND,APP,ITERATION,BASELINE_DTR,CUs,FEEDBACK,COMMITS
ITR.FEEDBACK_DIR=ALONGSIDE_ITR — FEEDBACK file sits next to the ITR file in itr-buffer/: same directory, same basename, .feedback extension. Both files are overwritten each iteration, never appended. Previous versions are in git history.
LAYER.ORDER=DOMAIN,APPLICATION,INFRASTRUCTURE,CONTROL
LAYER.DOMAIN=MODELS_ONLY — entities, value objects, no logic, no infrastructure imports
LAYER.APPLICATION=SERVICES_PORTS_USECASES — operational logic, business rules, port interfaces
LAYER.INFRASTRUCTURE=ENVIRONMENT_SINGLETON_ADAPTERS_DOTENV — config, dotenv walk-up discovery and loading, IO, persistence, external APIs
LAYER.CONTROL=CONTAINER_CONTROLLERS_CLI_ENTRYPOINT — dependency injection, controllers, CLI, main
ITR_GEN.INPUT=DTR,ADV,DSG
ITR_GEN.LEGEND=ITRs must self-declare all symbols: ITR.LEGEND=> flow, X exchange, + combine, ${} expansion, CRITICAL severity marker, | item separator, CU computational unit
ITR_GEN.STEP1=RESOLVE_TARGETS_FROM_BASELINE — Coder parses baseline DTR and maps targeted CUs to existing addresses or paths.
ITR_GEN.STEP2=IMPLEMENT_CUS — Implement targeted CUs (classes, methods, modules) in dependency order. Follow exact implementation instructions.
ITR_GEN.STEP3=DECLARE_DTR_DELTAS — Expose the expected types, methods, and relation signatures specified in CU.ID.NEW_DTR_LINES.
ITR_GEN.STEP4=VERIFY_DTR_DELTAS — Run dtr-builder on the newly modified code. Statically verify that the newly generated DTR contains all lines declared in NEW_DTR_LINES.
ITR_GEN.STEP5=WRITE_CODER_FEEDBACK — Coder OVERWRITES the FEEDBACK file alongside the ITR. Same directory, same basename, .feedback extension. Fields include: ITR_ID, CODER_NAME, DATE, CLARITY_RATING, AMBIGUOUS_LINES, MISSING_CONTEXT, ARCHITECTURE_DEVIATION, COMMIT_MESSAGE, TIME_TAKEN. Coder must provide their own descriptive COMMIT_MESSAGE summarizing the implemented changes.
ITR_GEN.STEP6=GENERATE_COMMITS — Call commit tool with CODER'S OWN descriptive message from FEEDBACK.COMMIT_MESSAGE. Commit includes changed code, ITR, FEEDBACK, and modified sys tensor. Never skip.
ITR_GEN.OUTPUT=STRICT_CU_ORDER — Coder must follow CU dependency sequence. DTR verification is mandatory.
ARCH.CONSTRAINTS=HEX,DI,DIP,NO_CROSS_LAYER,PORT_FLOW_OUT_IN,DOTENV_WALKUP,CODER_FEEDBACK,SEVERITY,ITR_LIFECYCLE,HARD_FAIL,DTR_DELTA_VERIFICATION
ARCH.HEX=Hexagonal architecture — domain innermost, application defines ports, infrastructure provides adapters
ARCH.DI=Dependency injection — all dependencies provided from outside, no service locators
ARCH.DIP=Dependency inversion — high level modules own the interfaces, low level modules implement them
ARCH.NO_CROSS_LAYER=Each layer depends only on the layer directly below it
ARCH.PORT_FLOW=Outbound ports defined in application layer, inbound adapters in infrastructure layer
ARCH.DOTENV=DotEnv walk-up discovery is mandatory for every application. Infrastructure must include a DotEnvLoader that walks up from root to filesystem root, loading the first .env found. Supports KEY=VALUE parsing, single/double/unquoted values, composite ${VAR} expansion, recursive resolution (max depth 10), cycle detection. Not finding .env is not an error.
ARCH.DOTENV.MERGE=SYSTEM_OVERRIDES — system environment variables take precedence over .env values
ARCH.DOTENV.DISCOVERY=Walk up from application root toward filesystem root, check each directory for .env. First hit loads. None found = proceed with empty DotEnv.
ARCH.DOTENV.EXPANSION=Pattern ${VAR_NAME} inside values is replaced with VAR_NAME value. Multiple ${} per value supported. Depth limit 10. Circular and self-references produce hard error.
ARCH.DOTENV.QUOTING=Unquoted and double-quoted values expand ${}. Single-quoted values are literal — no expansion.
ARCH.ITR.LIFECYCLE=ONE_PER_APP,TRACKED_IN_GIT,OVERWRITE_EACH_ITERATION — each application has a single ITR file at itr-buffer/<app-name>.itr and a single FEEDBACK file at itr-buffer/<app-name>.feedback. Each iteration: the Advisor OVERWRITES the ITR, the Coder OVERWRITES the FEEDBACK. Git history preserves every version.
ARCH.ITR.LOCATION=itr-buffer/<app-name>.itr — one ITR file per application. Example: itr-buffer/dtr-builder.itr.
ARCH.FEEDBACK=Coder feedback is mandatory. It is a SEPARATE output file in itr-buffer/ alongside the ITR, not embedded in the ITR. Same basename as ITR, .feedback extension. Coder OVERWRITES it and prints the full content in their final message.
ARCH.FEEDBACK.FIELDS=ITR_ID,CODER_NAME,DATE,CLARITY_RATING,AMBIGUOUS_LINES,MISSING_CONTEXT,TOO_MUCH_DETAIL,ARCHITECTURE_DEVIATION,DOTENV_CLARITY,LANGUAGE_COVERAGE,STEP_ORDER_ISSUES,SUGGESTIONS,TIME_TAKEN,COMMIT_MESSAGE
ARCH.FEEDBACK.FILE_PATTERN=<ITR_BASENAME>.feedback in itr-buffer/ — one file per application, placed in the same directory as the ITR file. Path derived from ITR path by replacing .itr with .feedback.
ARCH.FEEDBACK.FORMAT=ITR tensor format: KEY=VALUE per line, one semantic unit per line
ARCH.FEEDBACK.RATING_SCALE=1-5 — 1=impossible to follow, 5=crystal clear, no questions
ARCH.FEEDBACK.TIME_TAKEN=Duration to implement targeted CUs from start to feedback creation. Unit: minutes.
ARCH.FEEDBACK.REQUIRED_BEFORE_COMMIT=Coder must write FEEDBACK file with severity self-assessment and explicit COMMIT_MESSAGE before executing ITR_GEN.STEP6 (GENERATE_COMMITS). Missing feedback or commit message = hard fail.
ARCH.FEEDBACK.TRACKING=Git history. FEEDBACK files are committed alongside ITRs and code. Previous iterations are visible via git log.
ARCH.SEVERITY=CRITICAL,MAJOR,MINOR,TRIVIAL — standard LLMDD severity taxonomy for evaluating implementation fidelity to ITR spec
ARCH.SEVERITY.CRITICAL=Stub instead of real implementation. Missing core feature. DIP/Dependency inversion violation. Exposing different DTR signature than declared in NEW_DTR_LINES. Appending to FEEDBACK instead of overwriting. Hard fail — coder MUST stop and report to Designer.
ARCH.SEVERITY.MAJOR=Feature implemented but differs from spec in significant way. Wrong layer placement. Incorrect DI wiring. Must fix but non-blocking — can proceed after Designer acknowledges.
ARCH.SEVERITY.MINOR=Functional but differs from spec in approach. Different library choice. Naming conventions. Acceptable with note in FEEDBACK.
ARCH.SEVERITY.TRIVIAL=Documentation, comments, formatting, whitespace. Nice to fix but not required.
ARCH.HARD_FAIL=Hard fail on any CRITICAL or MAJOR constraint violation — stop and report. CRITICAL requires Designer guidance before proceeding.
ARCH.DTR_DELTA_VERIFICATION=Statically verify Coder compliance. The post-implementation DTR must contain all types, signatures, and relations declared in each CU's NEW_DTR_LINES. Discrepancy is SEVERITY:CRITICAL.
RULE.DTR=POSITIONAL,FLAT,NO_TREE,EXPLICIT_RELATIONS,DETERMINISTIC
RULE.ADV=ANALYZE_ONLY,NO_IMPLEMENTATION
RULE.ADV.ITR=Every ITR emitted by the Advisor OVERWRITES the existing ITR file at itr-buffer/<app>.itr. Before overwriting, the Advisor verifies the previous version is committed in git HEAD (no dirty ITR file). If uncommitted, hard fail — Designer must commit first. Advisor tags each ITR deliverable with implicit SEVERITY:CRITICAL unless explicitly marked otherwise. Advisor defines the CUs, target addresses, and expected NEW_DTR_LINES for delta verification.
RULE.ADV.REWRITE_ITR=Before emitting a new ITR, the Advisor ensures the previous itr-buffer/<app>.itr is committed in git HEAD. The Advisor then overwrites the file with the new ITR content and commits it before the Coder session begins.
RULE.DSG=EMIT_ITR_ONLY,NO_CODE
RULE.COD=EXECUTE_ITR_ONLY,NO_DESIGN_CHANGE,STRICT_CU_ORDER,AUTO_COMMIT_ON_COMPLETE,WRITE_FEEDBACK_FILE,SELF_ASSESS_SEVERITY,COMMIT_ITR,OVERWRITE_FEEDBACK,VERIFY_DTR_DELTAS
RULE.COD.FEEDBACK=Coder OVERWRITES the FEEDBACK file. Must overwrite, never append. Coder self-assessess SEVERITY of each ARCHITECTURE_DEVIATION and provides a custom, descriptive COMMIT_MESSAGE summarizing the implemented changes. If any deviation is CRITICAL, Coder MUST report and stop for Designer guidance before commit.
RULE.COD.COMMIT_ITR=Coder must commit the ITR file and FEEDBACK file alongside application code changes. The commit message MUST be exactly the descriptive summary written in FEEDBACK.COMMIT_MESSAGE.
HOOK.TRIGGER=ON_ITR_COMPLETE
HOOK.ACTION=GIT_ADD_ALL_AND_COMMIT
HOOK.MESSAGE_TEMPLATE=CODER_PROVIDED_COMMIT_MESSAGE — the message written by the Coder in FEEDBACK.COMMIT_MESSAGE is used for the git commit
HOOK.CONDITION=ALL_STEPS_PASSED_INCLUDING_FEEDBACK_SEVERITY_DTR_VERIFICATION
PYTHON.MONADS=RETURNS_SAFE_AND_FUTURE_SAFE
PYTHON.PATTERN_MATCHING=MATCH_CASE_RESULTE_FUTURERESULTE_NO_TRY_CATCH
PYTHON.DATACLASSES=SLOTTED_FROZEN
PYTHON.TYPING=EXPLICIT_ALL_VARIABLES
PYTHON.BUILD=UV_PYPROJECT_TOML_PACKAGE
SCALA.BUILD=SBT
SCALA.EXECUTABLE=PREPEND_EXECUTION_SCRIPT — so binary is callable by name, no java -jar needed
SCALA.PACKAGING=FAT_JAR_SELF_CONTAINED
TYPESCRIPT.MONADS=EXPLICIT_MONAD_LIBRARIES
TYPESCRIPT.TYPING=EXPLICIT_ALL_VARIABLES
JAVA.MONADS=EXPLICIT_MONAD_LIBRARIES
JAVA.TYPING=EXPLICIT_ALL_VARIABLES
OPS=COMMIT,LOCK,RESOLVE_TARGETS,IMPLEMENT_CUS,VERIFY_DELTAS,WRITE_FEEDBACK,SEVERITY_ASSESS,COMMIT_ITR,AUTO_COMMIT
